## Context

The autonomous night pipeline has no scheduler. `systemctl --user list-timers
--all` knows three timers on this host and none of them is the nightbeat; the
two units sit in `systemd/` in this repository, uninstalled, without a commit
since 2026-05-13. The usage census over every local session trace explains four
zeros at once: `beat` 0 invocations, `nightbeat-report` 0, `nightbeat-supervisor`
2 (last 2026-07-11), `pick-ticket` 8 (last 2026-07-10). The block stopped being
exercised in mid-July and stopped being scheduled before that.

Keeping it in this state is the worst of both: it is ported, tested and
maintained while nothing triggers it. `tests/test_beat.py` is the largest test
file in the repository, 97 858 bytes, for the least used skill. The author's
decision (2026-09-09) is removal, not redeployment.

Tracked by 0876. Blocked by 0881, which removes a different set of skills and
touches the same generated catalog; parallel branches would conflict there.

## Relevant files

Removed:

- `skills/beat/`, `skills/nightbeat-report/`, `skills/nightbeat-supervisor/`,
  `skills/pick-ticket/` — 17 975 B
- `scripts/beat.py`, `nightbeat-report.py`, `nightbeat-supervisor-survey.py`,
  `supervisor-budget.py`, `migrate-supervisor-journal.py`, `beat-settings.json`
- `scripts/fewer-permission-prompts-helper.py` — zero executions in the window;
  its docstring names `beat.py` as its only caller
- `scripts/guard-no-push.sh` — never wired into any settings file, and its
  predicate is `BEAT_HOUSEKEEPING_PR`; it guards a mode that will not exist
- `systemd/claude-nightbeat-supervisor.{service,timer}`
- nine tests whose subject disappears, including `test_needs_human_screen.py`
  (exercises `pick-ticket` alone) and `test_housekeeping_git.py` (exercises the
  `beat-skip` expiry alone)

Edited, live:

- `skills/molt/SKILL.md` — loses its dual mode (see below)
- `scripts/housekeeping-git.sh` — `beat-skip` expiry has no producer left
- `scripts/skill-doctor-survey.py` — nightbeat log scan, supervisor journal and
  six entries of its failure catalogue
- `skills/raid`, `skills/hunt`, `skills/dream`, `skills/merge/erg-pr-merge`,
  `skills/skill-doctor`, `skills/reviewers/benchmark-board.yml`,
  `scripts/setup-claude-agent.sh`, `rules/workflow.md`, `README.md`,
  `settings.json`, `settings.shared.json` — references and permission entries

## The one behaviour change

`molt` (39 invocations, third most used housekeeping skill) branches on
`BEAT_HOUSEKEEPING_BRANCH` in five places — steps 1, 6.5, 68-69, 208 and
214-222 — to skip its git phase when `beat.py` has already run it. With
`beat.py` gone the variable is never set, so molt reduces to its interactive
mode. The author chose to make that explicit in this change rather than leave
the branches inert.

## Test

Three tests fail the moment the block is removed, and each failure is the
red step for one edit:

- `tests/test_hunt_worktree_ownership.py` asserts `"beat.py" in step3`
- `tests/test_dream.py:118` resolves `scripts/nightbeat-supervisor-survey.py`
- `tests/test_rename_orchestrator_to_raid.sh` greps `scripts/nightbeat-report.py`

Run the suite before editing them: the three failures prove the sweep reached
the live callers rather than only the dead files.

## Verification

- [ ] The three tests above fail before their edits and pass after
- [ ] No reference to the removed names survives outside `docs/` and `tickets/`
- [ ] `make check-skills-drift` passes after `make skills-catalog`
- [ ] `make check` passes
- [ ] `tickets/erg check tickets/` passes

## Invariants

- `molt` keeps working interactively; only its beat-driven path goes.
- No other live skill changes behaviour.
- `docs/` keeps its historical record of the nightbeat era untouched.

## Exit criteria

- The block is gone, the three broken tests are green, the suite is green, and
  no settings file still grants a permission for a script that no longer exists.
